<title>LITHUANIA: LITHUANIA-BOURSE CAPITALISATION FELL LAST WEEK.</title>
<headline>LITHUANIA-BOURSE CAPITALISATION FELL LAST WEEK.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The capitalisation of the Vilnius</p>
<p>bourse continued to slide and dipped to 5.418 billion litas last</p>
<p>week from 5.600 billion litas the previous week, the stock</p>
<p>exchange said on Monday.</p>
<p>Vilnius bourse statistics:</p>
<p>					     May 19-23     May 12-16</p>
<p>    Submitted orders		   20,563	  20,469</p>
<p>    Executed orders		    1,999	   1,692</p>
<p>Number of transactions on</p>
<p>    Central market (CM)		1,255	   1,464</p>
<p>    Turnover on the CM in LTL	3,454,120     3,723,950</p>
<p>Number of transactions in</p>
<p>    block trades (BT)		  372	     112</p>
<p>    Turnover of BT in LTL	    13,520,330    4,143,750</p>
<p>    Supply of shares per week	58,674,300    53,912,443</p>
<p>    Demand of shares per week	29,076,760    20,445,999</p>
<p>Turnover of shares</p>
<p>    on CM per week in LTL	    3,425,520     3,620,500</p>
<p>    in BT per week in LTL	    9,694,440     3,961,440</p>
<p>The number of transactions</p>
<p>    in government T-bills	    7		 5</p>
<p>The turnover of government</p>
<p>    T-bills in LTL per week	  3,854,490     285,770</p>
<p>-- Andrius Vilkancas, Vilnius newsroom + 370 2 22 35 17</p>
